# Schema Relationships

This diagram projects explicit owning relations from schema fields. Inverse relation fields are not emitted again, avoiding duplicate edges.

```mermaid
erDiagram
{% set state = namespace(edges=0) %}
{% for schema in schemas %}
{% for field in schema.fields %}
{% if field.relation %}
{% set state.edges = state.edges + 1 %}
    {{ schema.name.pascal }} {% if field.relation.is.one_to_one %}||--||{% elif field.relation.is.one_to_many %}||--o{{% elif field.relation.is.many_to_many %}}o--o{{{% else %}}o--||{% endif %} {{ field.relation.target.schema.name.pascal }} : "{{ field.name.raw }}"
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% if state.edges == 0 %}
    EMPTY {
        string note "No explicit schema relations"
    }
{% endif %}
```

The diagram is semantic documentation only. Database-specific foreign-key names, junction tables, and ORM navigation details belong to persistence packs.
